## psc/driver/target.pengu — modelo de target de compilación.
##
## Un `Target` describe para qué plataforma se compila. En este MVP se aceptan
## el host nativo y `wasm32-unknown-emscripten` (alias `wasm`, `wasm32`,
## `emscripten`). `wasm32-wasi` se reconoce para poder rechazarlo con un mensaje
## claro, y cualquier otro triple de cross-compilación se rechaza hasta que el
## driver tenga soporte real.
##
## ## Memoria
## Todos los strings son owned; liberar con `free`.

import std.rites
import std.scrolls as scrolls

import psc.sema.names as npool
import psc.sema.options as sopts
import psc.codegen.options as cgopt

insignia psc_driver_target_

## Plataforma de compilación.
##
## ## Memoria
## Strings owned; liberar con `free`.
rune Target:
    ## `true` si el texto se pudo interpretar.
    ok as bool
    ## Error de parseo (owned) cuando `ok` es `false`.
    error as string
    ## Texto original tal y como lo pasó el usuario (vacío = host).
    raw as string
    ## Triple canónico (`wasm32-unknown-emscripten` o `""` para host).
    triple as string
    ## SO de compilación (`linux`, `macos`, `windows`, `emscripten`).
    os as string
    ## Arquitectura (`x64`, `arm64`, `x86`, `arm`, `wasm32`).
    arch as string
    ## Entorno del triple (`gnu`, `musl`, `mingw`, `emscripten`, `wasi`, ...).
    env as string
    ## `true` si el target es WebAssembly.
    is_wasm as bool
    ## `""` nativo, `emscripten` o `wasi`.
    wasm_target as string
    ## `true` si coincide con el host.
    is_host as bool

## Copia owned de un string.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave copy with s as string into string:
    return calling npool.copy_string with s

## Normaliza un nombre de arquitectura a la ortografía del compilador.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave arch_name with s as string into string:
    if s == "x86_64" or s == "amd64":
        return calling copy with "x64"
    if s == "aarch64" or s == "arm64":
        return calling copy with "arm64"
    if s == "i386" or s == "i686":
        return calling copy with "x86"
    if s == "wasm32" or s == "wasm":
        return calling copy with "wasm32"
    return calling copy with s

## SO del host en el vocabulario de `Target`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave host_os into string:
    var u as string is calling rites.uname
    var out as string is "linux"
    if u == "Windows":
        set out is "windows"
    else if u == "Darwin":
        set out is "macos"
    banish u
    return calling copy with out

## Copia owned de un target.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve strings owned; liberar con `free`.
weave clone with t as Target into Target:
    return with ok is t.ok, error is (calling copy with t.error), raw is (calling copy with t.raw), triple is (calling copy with t.triple), os is (calling copy with t.os), arch is (calling copy with t.arch), env is (calling copy with t.env), is_wasm is t.is_wasm, wasm_target is (calling copy with t.wasm_target), is_host is t.is_host

## Target del host.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve strings owned; liberar con `free`.
weave host into Target:
    var osn as string is calling host_os
    var ar as string is calling rites.host_arch
    return with ok is true, error is "", raw is "", triple is "", os is osn, arch is ar, env is "", is_wasm is false, wasm_target is "", is_host is true

## Target wasm canónico.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve strings owned; liberar con `free`.
weave wasm_target with which as string, raw_text as string into Target:
    var triple as string is "wasm32-unknown-emscripten"
    var env as string is "emscripten"
    if which == "wasi":
        set triple is "wasm32-wasi"
        set env is "wasi"
    return with ok is true, error is "", raw is (calling copy with raw_text), triple is triple, os is "emscripten", arch is "wasm32", env is env, is_wasm is true, wasm_target is (calling copy with which), is_host is false

## Target de error.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve strings owned; liberar con `free`.
weave failed with msg as string into Target:
    return with ok is false, error is msg, raw is "", triple is "", os is "", arch is "", env is "", is_wasm is false, wasm_target is "", is_host is false

## Interpreta `--target` / `[build] target`.
##
## Acepta `""` (host), `wasm`, `wasm32`, `emscripten`,
## `wasm32-unknown-emscripten`, `wasm32-wasi`/`wasi`, y triples del host.
## Cualquier otro triple se rechaza: el driver todavía no hace cross-compilation
## nativa real.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve strings owned; liberar con `free`.
weave parse with text as string into Target:
    var trimmed as string is calling scrolls.trim with text
    defer banish trimmed
    if trimmed length == 0:
        return calling host
    var raw as string is calling copy with trimmed
    var low as string is calling scrolls.to_lower with trimmed
    defer banish low
    if (low == "wasm" or low == "wasm32" or low == "emscripten") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "emscripten"):
        banish raw
        return calling wasm_target with "emscripten", text
    if (low == "wasi") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "wasi"):
        banish raw
        return calling wasm_target with "wasi", text
    # Triple nativo: se acepta si coincide con el host. El cruce real
    # Linux ⇄ Windows queda fuera del MVP y se rechaza explícitamente.
    var osn as string is "linux"
    var env as string is ""
    if (calling scrolls.contains with low, "windows") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "mingw") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "msvc"):
        set osn is "windows"
    else if (calling scrolls.contains with low, "darwin") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "macos") or (calling scrolls.contains with low, "apple"):
        set osn is "macos"
    else if (calling scrolls.contains with low, "linux"):
        set osn is "linux"
    if calling scrolls.contains with low, "mingw":
        set env is "mingw"
    else if calling scrolls.contains with low, "msvc":
        set env is "msvc"
    else if calling scrolls.contains with low, "musl":
        set env is "musl"
    else if calling scrolls.contains with low, "gnu":
        set env is "gnu"
    var first_end as int is low length
    var fi as int is 0
    while fi < low length:
        var ch as string is low at fi
        if ch == "-":
            banish ch
            set first_end is fi
            break
        banish ch
        set fi is fi + 1
    var first as string is low at 0 to first_end
    var ar as string is calling arch_name with first
    var hos as string is calling host_os
    var har as string is calling rites.host_arch
    var same as bool is (osn == hos) and (ar == har) and (env == "" or env == "gnu")
    banish hos
    banish har
    if not same:
        var msg as string is "target '{text}' is not supported; use the host or 'wasm32-unknown-emscripten' (native cross-compilation is not implemented yet)"
        banish ar
        banish first
        banish raw
        return calling failed with msg
    var out as Target is with ok is true, error is "", raw is raw, triple is "", os is osn, arch is ar, env is env, is_wasm is false, wasm_target is "", is_host is true
    banish first
    return out

## Libera un target.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera todos los strings.
weave free with t as ref to Target into void:
    banish t->error
    banish t->raw
    banish t->triple
    banish t->os
    banish t->arch
    banish t->env
    banish t->wasm_target

## Aplica un target a las opciones semánticas (copia owned de los strings).
##
## ## Memoria
## Reemplaza los strings owned de `o`; el llamador conserva el target.
weave apply_sema with t as Target, o as ref to sopts.SemaOptions into void:
    banish o->os_name
    set o->os_name is calling copy with t.os
    banish o->arch
    set o->arch is calling copy with t.arch
    banish o->wasm_target
    set o->wasm_target is calling copy with t.wasm_target
    if t.is_wasm:
        banish o->compiler
        set o->compiler is calling copy with "emcc"

## Aplica un target a las opciones de codegen (strings prestados).
##
## El target debe sobrevivir al codegen; el llamador lo garantiza.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna; asigna vistas.
weave apply_cg with t as Target, o as ref to cgopt.CgOptions into void:
    set o->wasm is t.is_wasm
    set o->wasm_target is t.wasm_target
    set o->target_triple is t.triple
    set o->os_name is t.os
    set o->arch is t.arch
